  "questions": [
    {
      "id": "cat-varc-1",
      "examSlug": "cat",
      "sectionId": "varc",
      "stimulusId": "cat-rc-1",
      "topic": "Reading Comprehension",
      "difficulty": "medium",
      "type": "mcq-single",
      "stem": {
        "type": "doc",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Which of the following best captures the central argument of the passage?"
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "a",
          "body": {
            "type": "doc",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Professions are superior to crafts because their knowledge can be taught systematically."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "b",
          "body": {
            "type": "doc",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Formalising a craft makes its knowledge portable but discards the part of it that resists being written down."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "c",
          "body": {
            "type": "doc",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Craftsmen are better practitioners than professionals because they learn by watching rather than by instruction."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "d",
          "body": {
            "type": "doc",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "The distinction between crafts and professions is arbitrary and reflects social status rather than knowledge."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "correct": {
        "kind": "options",
        "optionIds": [
          "b"
        ]
      },
      "solution": {
        "type": "doc",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "The passage grants professionalisation a real benefit — portability — and then argues it is bought at an uncounted cost, the tacit knowledge that cannot be written down. (B) carries both halves."
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "(A) and (C) each take only one side and turn it into a ranking the passage never makes. (D) contradicts the passage, which treats the distinction as substantive and locates it precisely."
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
